    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Classic microglandular adenosis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Microglandular adenosis glands are devoid of myoepithelium but are surrounded by a complete layer of basement membrane. Small eosinophilic secretions are often present in the lumina.",
    "source": "Edi Brogi",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/84/15/51767.jpg",
